message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Gaussian-kernel plug-and-play iterations can be unstable: a sharp dimension threshold for irreducible unit-diagonal kernels, the role of the mixing gap, and why unit diagonals matter"
version: 1.0.0-candidate
date-released: 2026-10-27
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23690125
authors:
  - name: Anonymous
license: CC0-1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ipitchford/gaussian-pnp-stability"
url: "https://evidencepress.org/releases/gaussian-pnp-stability/"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. Answers the open question of Sinha et al. (IEEE TSP 2025, Sec. II-A) for PnP-ISTA and PnP-ADMM with row-normalised kernel denoisers: irreducible unit-diagonal kernels with constant-preserving Hessians are stable in dimensions one to three and can be unstable in dimension four (explicit Gaussian family, exact certificates); a positive convolution example fails for very small steps; without unit diagonals failure occurs in dimension three. The divergence is extremely slow (at most about 1.7e-5 per iteration). Safe steps scale with the mixing gap; symmetrised denoisers are stable."
keywords:
  - plug-and-play
  - kernel denoiser
  - non-local means
  - Schur stability
  - PnP-ISTA
  - PnP-ADMM
  - mixing gap
  - exact certificate
